  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the man as the winner of the game",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the man playing the game, as the text 'I win again!' is directly overlaid on his image, creating an implicit identification of the user with the man as the winner. This projection is reinforced by the context of the 'Parkinson's disease game center' text, which frames the game as a therapeutic activity related to the condition. The user is not explicitly addressed with deictic pronouns like 'you' or 'me', but the first-person plural 'I' in the text creates a direct identification with the man's action, leading to a semiotic projection where the user sees themselves as the winner or participant in this context.",
